ed higher. The market prices in expectations and guidance, not just the headline number."},{"role":"heading","name":"How did results and stock reactions combine this season?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Of 467 reports with both a consensus and a non-flat next-day move: beat and rose 206 (44%), beat but fell 201 (43%), missed but rose 23 (5%), missed and fell 37 (8%)."},{"role":"heading","name":"How far into the season are we?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"481 of 503 S&P 500 companies (96%) have reported, with a next-day price reaction recorded for 484 reports. Data through 2026-09-30."},{"role":"heading","name":"Does a bigger beat mean a bigger stock move?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Not consistently. This season 56% of beats above +10% closed higher (149 reports), versus 52% of beats of 2% or less (54 reports). Large beats still failed to lift the stock in a meaningful share of cases; see the surprise-size table."},{"role":"heading","name":"How are these figures calculated?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Universe: current S&P 500 constituents. Season: calendar quarter of the release date. Beat rate: actual adjusted EPS above consensus adjusted EPS, among reports with a consensus. Price reaction: next regular-session close versus the prior close. Average move: mean absolute next-session return. See the methodology section."},{"role":"heading","name":"Can I cite this data?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Yes, with attribution to AFTERNS (afterns.com). A CSV of every underlying report is available on this page. Data and press inquiries: contact@afterns.com."},{"role":"heading","name":"When is US earnings season?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"It starts mid-January, mid-April, mid-July and mid-October and runs about four to six weeks. Across a year of AFTERNS data, 59.5% of all releases landed in just eight weeks."},{"role":"link","name":"Read the guide →","states":[{"name":"focusable","value":true}]},{"role":"heading","name":"Why do stocks fall on good earnings?","states":[{"name":"level","value":3}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Usually because the beat was already priced in, the market's real bar sat above the published consensus, or next-quarter guidance disappointed. Across 4,926 US reports, 45.4% of beats closed lower the next session."},{"role":"StaticText","name":"← "},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Previous season"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"AFTERNS INSIGHT"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"“"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"A quarter where strong results did not translate into stock gains."},{"role":"StaticText","name":"”"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Beats ran above the prior 7-season average, yet more of them were sold than usual."},{"role":"StaticText","name":"See the four outcomes"},{"role":"link","name":"Results × price","states":[{"name":"focusable","value":true}]},{"role":"link","name":"Sectors","states":[{"name":"focusable","value":true}]},{"role":"link","name":"Stocks","states":[{"name":"focusable","value":true}]},{"role":"link","name":"Trend · past seasons","states":[{"name":"focusable","value":true}]},{"role":"link","name":"Data · FAQ","states":[{"name":"focusable","value":true}]},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Beat and rose"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"median move"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"+3.5%"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Palantir Technologies Inc. Class A"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"+29.4%"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Zebra Technologies Corporation Class A"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"+26.5%"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Gartner Inc."},{"role":"StaticText","name":"+22.6%"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"-3.0%"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Applovin Corporation Class A"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"-19.7%"},{"role":"StaticText","name":"Datadog Inc. Class A"},{"role":